   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## instantid-character.json\n\nFace identity (InstantID)\n\nE14b - InstantID (SDXL). Facial identity measured against the reference portrait with insightface/antelopev2: cosine 0.823 vs Flux Kontext's 0.187. CAVEAT: InstantID transfers the FACE ONLY - clothing/design must come from the prompt. The composition used to bias toward a close-up bust even when the prompt asked for a full scene - the cause is NOT the face embedding: with `image_kps` unconnected, the keypoint ControlNet derives its keypoints FROM THE REFERENCE PORTRAIT, mirroring its framing (measured A/B, E14b addendum). `image_kps` (now wired, default = the same portrait) is the decoupler: point it at a full-body donor with a detectable face (>= ~112 px - we generated one at 1024 and upscaled 2x: `input/2d/kps_donor_body.png`) and the composition follows the donor while the face identity stays with `image`. Needs a visible face in the reference (>=~112 px); a full-body 1024 image gives only ~60 px, which is why portrait_heroine exists. weight 0.8, 30 steps, cfg 5.0, 30 s.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S7** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E14b** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## instantid-character.json\n\nFace identity (InstantID)\n\nE14b - InstantID (SDXL). Facial identity measured against the reference portrait with insightface/antelopev2: cosine 0.823 vs Flux Kontext's 0.187. CAVEAT: InstantID transfers the FACE ONLY - clothing/design must come from the prompt. The composition used to bias toward a close-up bust even when the prompt asked for a full scene - the cause is NOT the face embedding: with `image_kps` unconnected, the keypoint ControlNet derives its keypoints FROM THE REFERENCE PORTRAIT, mirroring its framing (measured A/B, E14b addendum). `image_kps` (now wired, default = the same portrait) is the decoupler: point it at a full-body donor with a detectable face (>= ~112 px - we generated one at 1024 and upscaled 2x: `input/2d/kps_donor_body.png`) and the composition follows the donor while the face identity stays with `image`. Needs a visible face in the reference (>=~112 px); a full-body 1024 image gives only ~60 px, which is why portrait_heroine exists. weight 0.8, 30 steps, cfg 5.0, 30 s.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S7** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E14b** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   },
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  },
